   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## several projectors \u00b7 blend masks\n\n**You need:** Blender 4.x. No AI models.\n\n**Your own model:** paste the path of your .blend / .fbx / .obj / .abc / .glb / .usd into `file` of both **scene render** nodes (Explorer: right click the file, Copy as path). Empty = the sample building.\n\n**Do:** Queue. Two upright projectors (1200 x 1600) stand 30 m in front of the sample model, 11 m apart, each covering a\nbit more than half of the facade. Each one gets its own scene render (same file, another projector). **projector\nblend** finds where both pictures land on the same stone and fades each one out towards its own border, so the\nlight adds up evenly: one mask per projector, in its picture size.\n\n**Use the masks:** multiply each projector's frames with its mask, or load the saved PNG as the blend mask of that\noutput in the media server. The regions, plan and sampler run once per projector on its own scene render.\n\n**Then try:** a third and fourth projector (scene_3, scene_4); `ramp` larger for a softer blend (the overlap must be\nat least that wide); projectors at different heights or turned (`turn_deg`) for a corner of a building.\n"
   ],
   "title": "read me"
  }
